    {
      "id": "81609f3d80975afe",
      "text": "Ukrainian ⁠President Volodymyr Zelensky said ⁠on Sunday he had spoken to US President Donald Trump and the two agreed to meet in New York for ‌talks that “could change a lot” in terms of finding a resolution to the war with Russia that began in February 2022.\nThe two leaders will be in New York in the coming week for the UN ⁠General Assembly.\n“We agreed to meet in New York, ‌and this meeting could change a lot. There is diplomatic momentum,” Zelensky wrote ‌on social media.\nZelensky said he...",
