    {
      "id": "d9fca56702b3cff5",
      "text": "German Chancellor Friedrich Merz suffered a bruising electoral setback in two state elections on Sunday, including a historic defeat for his party, but vowed to press ahead with potentially painful reforms to Europe’s biggest economy.\nExit polls by public broadcaster ARD on Sunday night indicated that Merz’s centre-right Christian Democratic Union, or CDU, came in with just 5 per cent in Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania – the lowest result ever since World War II for the party in any state. The...",
      "title": "Germany’s Merz vows to press ahead with reforms after historic state election defeat",
      "url": "https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3368175/germanys-merz-vows-press-ahead-reforms-after-historic-state-election-defeat?utm_source=rss_feed",
